<title>THAILAND: Thai rubber exports reach 1.72 mln tonnes in 1996.</title>
<headline>Thai rubber exports reach 1.72 mln tonnes in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai rubber exports rose to about 1.72 million tonnes in 1996 from 1.68 million in 1995, an agriculture ministry official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said the 1996 exports earned Thailand about 60.97 billion baht ($2.43 billion) in foreign exchange against 60.24 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>The official said slow rubber exports in the first six months of 1996 picked up in the second half of last year.</p>
<p>Thailand, the world biggest natural rubber producer, estimated its 1996 output at 1.88 million tonnes and expects to raise its annual production to 2.2-2.5 million during the years 2000-2010.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
